# Multiple Regression

## Multiple Regression

So far, we've only examined the relationship between a continuous outcome and continuous predictor one at a time with *simple regression*. With *multiple regression*, we can examine these relationships **jointly**: looking at one relationship while adjusting for the relationships of other variables.

$$y_i = \beta_0 \, + \, \beta_1 x_{1i} \, + \, \beta_2 x_{2i} \, + \, ... \, + \, \beta_p x_{2i} \, + \, \epsilon$$

::: subpoint
○ $\beta_0$: value of $y$ when *all predictors* $x = 0$
:::

::: subpoint
○ $\beta_1$: slope of $x_{1i}$ adjusted for the effect of $x_{2i}, \, ..., \,x_{pi}$ 
:::


## Simple Regression

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(palmerpenguins)

m1 <- lm(body_mass_g ~ bill_depth_mm, data = penguins) 
summary(m1)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```

Call:
lm(formula = body_mass_g ~ bill_depth_mm, data = penguins)

Residuals:
     Min       1Q   Median       3Q      Max 
-1607.38  -510.10   -66.96   462.43  1819.28 

Coefficients:
              Estimate Std. Error t value Pr(>|t|)    
(Intercept)    7488.65     335.22   22.34   <2e-16 ***
bill_depth_mm  -191.64      19.42   -9.87   <2e-16 ***
---
Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1

Residual standard error: 708.1 on 340 degrees of freedom
  (2 observations deleted due to missingness)
Multiple R-squared:  0.2227,	Adjusted R-squared:  0.2204 
F-statistic: 97.41 on 1 and 340 DF,  p-value: < 2.2e-16
```


:::
:::

:::

::: {.column width="50%"}
The estimated penguin body mass when bill depth is zero is 7488.65.

An increase in 1 mm in bill depth is associated with an -191.64 g increase in body mass.
:::
::::


## Standardizing

::: {style="font-size:80%"}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
penguins_cleaned <- penguins |>
  drop_na(bill_length_mm, bill_depth_mm, flipper_length_mm, body_mass_g) |>
  mutate(
    across(
      ends_with("_mm"), 
      function(col) (col - mean(col)) / sd(col), 
      .names = "{.col}_z")
    )
penguins_cleaned
```

